.nh
.TH "TEAMS" "1" "Oct 2026" "teams dev" "teams Manual"

.SH NAME
teams-unread - Show unread chats and the mentions you have not read


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBteams unread [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show what is waiting for you: chats whose newest message is newer than
their read watermark, and the messages that mention you. It never marks
anything read.

.PP
Both halves look at the last 24h by default; --since/--until change the
window and --all removes it, which lists every unread chat however old.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	every unread chat, however old (no window)

.PP
\fB--chats\fP[=false]
	only unread chats

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for unread

.PP
\fB--mentions\fP[=false]
	only unread mentions

.PP
\fB--since\fP=""
	window to look back over (default 24h; a duration or a timestamp)

.PP
\fB--until\fP=""
	ignore activity newer than this


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--jq\fP=""
	filter JSON output through a jq expression (implies --json)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also honours NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	never prompt; fail fast instead

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (default: the configured default_profile)

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress progress messages on stderr

.PP
\fB--read-only\fP[=false]
	refuse write commands

.PP
\fB--refresh\fP[=false]
	ignore cached names and resolve them again

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	verbose diagnostics on stderr (-v, -vv)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBteams(1)\fP
